    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d688">

                <pb facs="1026" n="894" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg894"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.512/433: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Mayer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-10-30T11:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 30,
                                1926—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 31—2:15
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>521. My 520, October 30, 2 p.m., paragraph 1.</p>
                <p>[1.] Following from American consul general, Canton: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“October 30, 1 p.m. Your October 29, 11 a.m.<anchor n="77"
                                xml:id="d688-f1"/> I have concurred in the protest against the
                            inspection regulations which the senior [apparent omission] will now
                            hand to Chen.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>2. Jenkins resumed charge on the 30th.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mayer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
